       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day, and 1,200 mg/day is the usual limit for OTC use). A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum for inpatient anti-inflammatory dosing)\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses (for example, 400 mg four times daily)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that the dose was intentional. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and frequency and I'll enter it now."
