     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're the attending and that you've confirmed the dose. But 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the labeled maximum, and I know of no indication that supports it. Extra dosing past about 3,200 mg/day adds toxicity (GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events) without adding efficacy. I don't want to put an order in the system that I think could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose, with a note if you like.\n- Enter another dose and frequency you choose that is within the labeled range.\n- Help you with an alternative if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen, or a different agent.\n\nIf you think this dose is necessary, for example under a specific protocol or trial, you can enter it directly in the order-entry system. It will then go through pharmacy verification and the hospital's dose-range checks. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
